<title>GERMANY: German Aug trade surplus down compared to July.</title>
<headline>German Aug trade surplus down compared to July.</headline>
<dateline>WIESBADEN, Germany 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistics Office reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p>			     (in billions of marks)</p>
<p> GERMAN TRADE/CURRENT ACC  Aug 96   July 96	  Aug 95</p>
<p> Trade balance		 +8.1    +10.3	    +6.9</p>
<p> Current account	     -4.6     -5.0	    -5.3</p>
<p> Exports			 58.4     69.1	    56.9</p>
<p> Imports			 50.3     58.8	    50.0</p>
<p> Services			-5.7     -6.7	    -7.7</p>
<p> Wage and property income  -0.8     -3.7	    +1.0</p>
<p> Transfers		     -5.9     -4.7	    -5.1</p>
<p> Supplementary trade	 -0.3     -2.2	    -0.4</p>
<p> GERMAN TRADE/CURRENT ACC  Jan-Aug 96	Jan-Aug 95</p>
<p> Trade balance		  +60.8	     +53.6</p>
<p> Current account		-21.5	     -18.7</p>
<p> Exports			  509.2	     489.6</p>
<p> Imports			  448.4	     436.0</p>
<p> Services			 -36.6	     -39.2</p>
<p> Wage and property income    -6.0		+4.6</p>
<p> Transfers			-37.5	     -35.5</p>
<p> Supplementary trade	   -2.2		-2.2</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49 228 26097150</p>
</text>
